        "blind_spot": "All failing kernels look uniformly 'DRAM-bound', but the metrics cannot distinguish block-barrier phase serialization (why DRAM sits at 66-86% on reduction kernels) from a lean-at-roofline vs instruction-bloated instruction stream, so the optimizer applies the same traffic-reduction template and either stalls at the roofline or regresses by adding sync/instruction overhead.",
        "rationale": {
          "smsp__warp_issue_stalled_barrier_per_warp_active.pct": "HIGH -> restructure reductions: warp-level reduction, more/smaller blocks to overlap load and compute phases, prefetch across phases / LOW -> block structure is fine, only pursue byte-count reduction, do not touch synchronization",
